WEBVTT

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:04.570
The final round in the West Japan 
Master Qualifiers...

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.850
Murao Shinichi versus Wataya Arata.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:10.130
It's a showdown between 
Nagumo Society members.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:15.860
<b>Hee Hee Hee</b>

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:13.020
That's truly a match-up worthy of the finals.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:16.210
Murao-kun was in a slump for a while,
but he's back on his feet.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:17.960
Shinichi-niichan!

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:23.990
<i>Murao-kun has really been showing off
 his experience and finesse lately.</i>

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:25.990
<i>But...</i>

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:29.750
<i>The one who seems more likely to prevent 
Master Suo's fifth win in a row is...</i>

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:48.150
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:49.980
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:56.470
Verse 10

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:56.470
Scarlet 
kadsuras

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:57.020
You have fifteen minutes of memorization time.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:59.020
The match will begin at 6:10.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.930
E-Excuse me...

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.990
<i>I'm never eating Yuu's cooking again.</i>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:20.300
<i>But what's causing this? 
The katsu? The katsuobushi?</i>

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.990
<b>East Japan Semifinals

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:28.630
<i>Why did I feel relieved earlier?</i>

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:32.420
<i>Why did knowing Taichi lost make me sigh?</i>

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.010
I'm sorry about that.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:38.560
<i>Even in the final,</i>

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.130
<i>Murao-san is the same as always.</i>

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:43.420
<i>I should be, too.</i>

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:46.360
<i>Just play karuta like I always do.</i>

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.190
It's time.

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.300
<i>Do the usual.</i>

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:57.200
<i>Visualize that room.</i>

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.770
<i>All alone...</i>

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.130
<i>Murao-kun's fast!</i>

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:04.290
<i>He went for a one-syllable card
on Arata-kun's side!</i>

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:09.200
<i>I never asked to be treated colder 
than the winds of Mount Hatsuse</i>

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.270
<i>He split up his "Though I" and "Though my"</i>

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:15.590
<i>to counter Arata-kun's strong cross stroke.</i>

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:19.410
<i>Murao-san is the same as always.</i>

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.750
<i>Would this old...</i>

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:24.380
<i>As this trip...</i>

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:26.560
<i>And yet...</i>

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:29.870
<i>Why am I...</i>

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.300
<i>You're getting in my way, Taichi!</i>

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.140
<i>Why are you there?</i>

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:41.400
<i>Taichi has a way of being unfair.</i>

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:44.700
<i>And he's not particularly talented,
like Chihaya is.</i>

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:47.840
<i>Maybe I...</i>

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:53.410
<i>always looked down on Taichi in karuta.</i>

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.450
<i>On my own friend...</i>

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:11.570
<i>The hazed early dawn light 
comes not from the moon</i>

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:11.570
<i>Arata-kun's cover came too late?</i>

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:16.480
<i>What's wrong with him?</i>

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:20.150
<i>Arata's seemed off since the Yoshino Tournament.</i>

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:31.750
<i>now white robes hang to 
dry on Mount Amanokagu</i>

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:23.020
<i>This is my chance.</i>

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:25.930
<i>Arata's gotten a lot stronger.</i>

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:28.720
<i>If he came into this in top form,
I'd be in trouble.</i>

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:32.520
<i>But with him playing this poorly, I can win.</i>

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:34.570
<i>I wish I could...</i>

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:35.610
<i>This year is my chance.</i>

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:40.520
After I win my fifth consecutive title,
 I'm going to retire.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.290
<i>My last chance!</i>

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:02.500
Just a moment, please.

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:10.070
Yamashiro-san is reading for us. 
We can't waste that.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:13.140
Come back to us, Arata.

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:40.530
<i>have been so—</i>

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:42.570
<i>Who was that?</i>

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:43.580
<i>The Queen again?</i>

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:46.440
<i>Re...</i>

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:48.660
<i>Really? At a time like this?!</i>

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:49.820
<i>Arata-kun?!</i>

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:53.440
S-Sorry... Excuse me!

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:54.770
<i>He left his seat!</i>

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:55.410
<i>The bathroom?!</i>

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:57.460
<i>In the middle of a match?!</i>

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:01.680
Coach, what happens now? 
What about the match?

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:03.640
Nothing happens.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:06.710
Cards will continue to be read, 
even if his opponent's not there.

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:09.010
<i>Note that though...</i>

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:10.770
<i>Unbelievable!</i>

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.330
<i>Running to the bathroom during a match?!</i>

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:13.570
<i>How many cards am I missing?</i>

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:15.270
<i>I have to hurry! Hurry!</i>

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:18.220
<i>Seriously, I'm never eating 
Yuu's cooking again!</i>

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.070
<i>Never again, Yuu, you idiot!</i>

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:21.660
<i>You idiot!</i>

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:23.040
My mom made it.

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:26.610
I wouldn't mind joining your karuta club.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:29.180
What kind of puny reward 
for winning is that?

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:31.020
<i>I was such a jerk.</i>

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:34.000
<i>Sorry, Yuu.</i>

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.750
<i>I'm nothing special at all.</i>

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:42.490
I'm sorry about that.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:52.500
<i>Four cards have gone
while I was in the bathroom.</i>

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:53.790
<i>I'm behind by eleven now.</i>

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:55.810
<i>How many dead cards were there?</i>

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:57.600
<i>What was read?</i>

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:01.830
<i>I'm losing to Murao-san by eleven cards...</i>

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:11.080
<i>I've never visualized myself coming 
back from a place like this to win.</i>

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:13.070
<i>But... what is this?</i>

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:14.810
<i>What is it?</i>

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:17.310
<i>I can't let this match go.</i>

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:23.150
<i>Even if I'm embarrassed,
even if I'm nothing special...</i>

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:24.620
<i>I can't run away.</i>

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:27.830
<i>He's down by eleven.</i>

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:30.510
<i>It'll be tough to recover from that,
even for Wataya-kun.</i>

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:33.640
<i>And it's more than just the differential at play.</i>

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:38.190
<i>The rule is that no one can tell him 
what was read while he was out.</i>

00:07:38.730 --> 00:07:42.980
<i>He doesn't know how many dead cards were read
in addition to the four on the board,</i>

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:46.260
<i>or how the unique syllables have changed.</i>

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:49.810
<i>This handicap goes far beyond 
just the differential.</i>

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:53.250
<i>I'm sure Arata-kun will 
do all he can, but...</i>

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:55.330
<i>This match is already...</i>

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:57.210
I'm going to move my cards.

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:07.460
<i>Arata...</i>

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:09.710
<i>He hasn't given up.</i>

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:15.160
<i>Considering the amount of time I was away,</i>

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:16.850
<i>there must've been two or three dead cards.</i>

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:19.790
<i>It's no use thinking about it.</i>

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:21.710
<i>I just have to keep going 
with what I do know.</i>

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:24.060
<i>Should I attack?</i>

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.480
<i>I'm afraid of faults and 
double faults, though.</i>

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:27.970
<i>I just have to do this.</i>

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.270
<i>Everyone's watching.</i>

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:32.190
<i>I can't make any more 
embarrassing mistakes.</i>

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:34.100
<i>I have to do this!</i>

00:08:35.230 --> 00:08:36.980
<i>Gust of wind...</i>

00:08:38.610 --> 00:08:41.100
<i>What a time for a one-syllable 
card on his own side!</i>

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:42.230
<i>That was lucky!</i>

00:08:44.020 --> 00:08:49.940
<i>It must be nice to have
28 one-syllable cards, Suo-san.</i>

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:53.170
<i>hence the name fall leaves</i>

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:52.880
<i>Wait, was it 27?</i>

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:59.540
<i>Even the Master says some 
random stuff sometimes.</i>

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.810
<b>Munch Munch</b>

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.810
<b>Fine 
Confections 
Kogetsuan</b>

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:02.950
<i>I don't care if I embarrass myself anymore.</i>

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:08.990
<i>For you, I head out to the 
fields to pick spring green</i>

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:08.380
<i>He jumped into the opponent's side
to cover "For you"!</i>

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:09.870
<i>No hesitation at all!</i>

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:11.810
<i>That's the usual Arata-kun.</i>

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:15.460
<i>A multi-syllable card right 
after a one-syllable card?</i>

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:17.870
<i>You're lucky, Arata.</i>

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:21.200
<i>But it won't last.</i>

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:24.630
<i>I have an overwhelming advantage
when it comes to two- and three-syllable cards.</i>

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:25.000
<i>Sone no Yoshitada 
Like a boatsman adrift at the mouth of the Yura, I do not know where this love will take me</i>

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:26.710
<i>Like a boatsman...</i>

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:27.670
<i>Murao-kun's fast!</i>

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:30.160
<i>Did he...</i>

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:32.340
<i>take that one after just hearing "Like"?</i>

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:37.040
<i>One of the dead cards was "Like the"!</i>

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:41.450
<i>Now there are only two dead cards 
I don't know about, at most.</i>

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:45.100
<i>Arata, visualize it.</i>

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:48.190
<i>The cards will tell me...</i>

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:53.320
<i>how to visualize myself winning.</i>

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:56.190
<b>Click   Click   Click</b>

00:09:54.990 --> 00:10:03.200
Silent Mode

00:09:56.190 --> 00:10:03.200
<b>Click   Click   Click</b>

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:59.640
<i>How are the Master qualifiers going?</i>

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:02.720
<i>I figured Wataya-kun would 
come out on top...</i>

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:03.200
<b>Not interested</b>

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:05.190
<i>But this is a tight match.</i>

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:08.390
<i>Megumu, Yuikawa-san's a 
tough opponent to play.</i>

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:12.210
<i>She's tough to play.</i>

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:13.210
<i>I never asked to be treated colder 
than the winds of Mount Hatsuse</i>

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.900
<i>She's unnaturally fast 
with her own left side.</i>

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:17.380
I'm moving my cards.

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:23.300
<i>She keeps moving more cards 
over from her right side.</i>

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.340
<i>She's hoping to take them 
all from her left!</i>

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:29.840
<i>A southpaw who excels
in defending her left side!</i>

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:34.920
<i>Sheesh... Another southpaw, 
just like the Queen?</i>

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:39.030
<i>I can't lose!</i>

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:40.110
<b>Click Click Click Click Click Click Click</b>

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:40.110
<b>Ba-dump</b>

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:42.980
<i>The tail feathers...</i>

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:44.730
<i>As I wait...</i>

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:47.750
<i>My only thought as the boat takes me...</i>

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:53.620
<i>Eleven cards versus eighteen... 
He's closing the gap.</i>

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:55.820
<i>Murao-san is staying calm.</i>

00:10:55.820 --> 00:10:59.210
<i>He's attacking the opponent's side,
which is standard when you have a big lead.</i>

00:10:59.210 --> 00:11:01.510
<i>But he looks really stressed out.</i>

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:08.780
<i>the cresting waves almost look 
like clouds in the skies</i>

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:07.800
<i>What...</i>

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:09.970
<i>is he worried about?</i>

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:12.220
<i>My fear is that you will forget...</i>

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:15.860
<i>He landed a clean cross on "My own home"
 and "My fear is that"!</i>

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:19.060
<i>"My fear is that" is the card Murao-kun 
sent him in the first half.</i>

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:20.900
<i>Of course!</i>

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:23.620
<i>He built an unbelievable lead over Arata-kun.</i>

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:28.700
<i>He was forced to send him cards he normally
never would have sent in the first half.</i>

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:33.670
<i>That meant giving "My own" and "My fear"
to Arata-kun, who has a strong cross stroke.</i>

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:36.980
<i>That's what's bothering Murao-kun now.</i>

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:38.920
<i>And he lost "My fear is that," too.</i>

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:43.320
<i>When you take a big lead over someone 
who's just as good as you,</i>

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:45.270
<i>it just stresses you out, even if you win.</i>

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:48.770
<i>Seventeen cards versus eleven...</i>

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:49.940
<i>I'm down by six.</i>

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:53.660
<i>It's not impossible. I can catch him.</i>

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:56.470
<i>I have to take this one card at a time.</i>

00:11:56.470 --> 00:11:58.150
<i>After I heard you say...</i>

00:11:58.730 --> 00:11:59.750
<i>He's attacking!</i>

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:00.350
<i>That was fast!</i>

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:05.880
<i>Of course I'm gonna be stressed out.</i>

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:08.460
<i>You're Wataya Arata, after all.</i>

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:14.030
<i>Ten versus seventeen.
I'm still seven cards ahead of Arata.</i>

00:12:14.780 --> 00:12:17.960
<i>I couldn't ask for better. 
I'm gonna keep attacking!</i>

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:22.090
<i>Murao-san...</i>

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:24.470
<i>The other dead card...</i>

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:27.120
<i>was "After I determined," wasn't it?</i>

00:12:31.240 --> 00:12:33.400
<i>I like how Murao-san plays karuta.</i>

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:38.350
<i>He's not swayed by what unfolds during a match.</i>

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:41.120
<i>His karuta is diligent and consistent.</i>

00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:46.610
<i>Said world grants no escape</i>

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:49.030
<i>Arata-kun crossed over both "Said world grants
no escape" and "Said world grants no change,"</i>

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:52.340
<i>but Murao-kun was guarding it from the side 
opposite where Arata-kun's hand came from!</i>

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:56.440
<i>"When there are two cards, 
I'll hold one down."</i>

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:59.030
<i>You can't make a move like that 
unless you make that decision.</i>

00:12:59.030 --> 00:13:01.080
<i>That's how Murao-kun counters Arata-kun!</i>

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:06.490
<i>Murao-san's definitely a tough opponent.</i>

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:32.430
<i>All right!</i>

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:34.610
<i>My offense is working. 
I'm getting cards from his side.</i>

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:37.380
<i>I can still move. I'm just fine.</i>

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:42.190
<i>My lead is down to four?</i>

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:42.930
<i>Already?</i>

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:50.430
<i>It's down to which cards are read.</i>

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:53.550
<i>Both of them are attacking 
the opponent's side,</i>

00:13:53.550 --> 00:13:55.490
<i>Nothing can be worse...</i>

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:56.740
<i>but most of the cards read 
are on Murao-kun's side.</i>

00:13:57.090 --> 00:14:01.760
<i>In terms of probability, more of the cards 
being read should be on Arata-kun's side,</i>

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:05.740
<i>yet he's attacking Murao-kun's side
with no fear whatsoever.</i>

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:06.950
<i>as my sleeves are wet with dew</i>

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:10.190
<i>Once he has a lead of more than ten cards,</i>

00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:14.430
<i>even Murao-san would only put his 
best cards closest to his hands.</i>

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:16.200
<i>Especially...</i>

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:18.370
<i>Swift waters parted...</i>

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:17.990
<i>on his right side!</i>

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:24.810
<i>Arata-kun usually plays with a 
balance of offense and defense,</i>

00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:26.520
<i>but he's attacking hard.</i>

00:14:27.890 --> 00:14:29.710
<i>He's calling the momentum to him.</i>

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:35.470
East Japan Qualifiers 
Dr. Harada 
(Winner)

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:35.480
<i>The momentum to fight</i>

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:39.100
<i>East Japan's number one,
the king of offensive karuta.</i>

00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:49.560
<i>Impassionate gods have never seen</i>

00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:48.980
<i>Murao-kun's fast, too!</i>

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:50.070
<i>He's keeping up!</i>

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:52.070
<i>Arata-kun was targeting 
"Impassionate," too!</i>

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:53.940
<i>Keep that lead, Shinichi-niichan!</i>

00:14:53.940 --> 00:14:56.410
<i>I want to beat Master Suo.</i>

00:14:57.290 --> 00:15:00.800
<i>He's beaten so many people on talent alone.</i>

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:04.300
<i>This is my last chance to 
beat him through hard work!</i>

00:15:08.110 --> 00:15:09.520
<i>Murao-san...</i>

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:12.880
<i>The last dead card that was read...</i>

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:15.300
<i>was "Impassioned vows"?</i>

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:21.440
<i>Hard work...</i>

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.830
<i>Talent...</i>

00:15:23.540 --> 00:15:24.880
<i>Hard work...</i>

00:15:25.300 --> 00:15:26.670
<i>Talent...</i>

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:29.330
<i>Hard work...</i>

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:33.210
<i>Talent...</i>

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:35.120
<i>banish any lingering memories of the past</i>

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:48.520
Thank you very much.

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.980
Thank you very much.

00:16:04.710 --> 00:16:05.480
Arata.

00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:11.980
Smile, Arata.

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:16.220
If you don't smile,
 I'm gonna get depressed.

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:22.310
Ow!

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:23.650
Don't actually smile, moron.

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:25.870
You'll make me even more depressed.

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:28.250
<b>Ha!</b>

00:16:27.160 --> 00:16:31.010
The winner of the final round,
 by two cards, is Wataya Arata-kun!

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:32.840
<i>I really like Murao-san.</i>

00:16:38.340 --> 00:16:40.570
You'd better win, Arata.

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:47.430
You've got both hard work 
and talent on your side.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:53.650
Certificate of Recommendation 
for Wataya Arata 
The above is hereby recommended to represent West Japan
in the play-off to decide the challenger for the 59th Master match. 
All Japan Karuta Association 
Chairman Mashita Yoshiaki

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:53.100
If I believe I do, I'll probably lose,

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:56.490
so I'm going to see someone who doesn't.

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:02.830
In the challenger play-offs 
to be held in November,

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:06.510
the representatives from West Japan will 
be Wataya Arata-kun for the Master title

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:08.770
and Ousaka Megumu-san for the Queen title.

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:16.090
Kyoto

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:18.710
Revolution!

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:19.970
Counter-revolution!

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:21.890
Go to sleep right now!

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:25.140
Is she gone? Is the Empress gone?

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:27.930
As if we could sleep. It's only eleven.

00:17:27.930 --> 00:17:29.340
Think we could sneak out?

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:30.930
To go where?

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:34.010
Class 3 made a game of sneaking out 
to go to the convenience store.

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:36.480
They got caught and had to sit in the hall.

00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:37.990
Wow!

00:17:40.520 --> 00:17:44.590
Sorry, Chi-chan! I still 
have your phone battery!

00:17:44.590 --> 00:17:45.710
Here.

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:47.830
It's fine.

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:50.340
Keep it until morning, Michiru-chan.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:51.590
I'll look if I have it.

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:58.980
<i>Chihaya-chan's a lot more considerate 
of others than everyone realizes.</i>

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:02.140
<i>She's really trying to 
focus on this class trip,</i>

00:18:02.990 --> 00:18:05.200
<i>even though she has other 
things on her mind.</i>

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:06.980
<i>Zzzz</i>

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:08.820
You're sleeping? What about girl talk?

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:10.870
I don't think Chi-chan is capable of that.

00:18:09.970 --> 00:18:13.220
Jeez, just change your good looks!
They're going to waste!

00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:13.220
Thanks, Chihaya-chan.

00:18:13.880 --> 00:18:15.480
I'm gonna go buy some tea.

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:17.430
Isn't the teacher standing out there?

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:19.490
They should at least let her get a drink.

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:33.440
Ta... Ta—

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:34.300
Shh!

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:36.290
Keep it down!

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:41.990
I felt better, so here I am.

00:18:41.990 --> 00:18:44.440
I didn't want to be at school taking 
supplementary lessons alone.

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:51.810
<i>Wh-What? Is she angry? Sad? Confused?</i>

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:55.510
A-Anyway, the Class 1 
boys are in that room.

00:18:55.510 --> 00:18:56.340
Okay.

00:18:56.340 --> 00:18:58.350
Ayase-san, go to bed.

00:18:58.350 --> 00:18:59.660
But... tea...

00:18:59.660 --> 00:19:01.330
I'll buy one for you.

00:19:01.330 --> 00:19:02.580
You stay in your room.

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:05.730
Night, Chihaya. You should 
get some sleep yourself.

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:11.210
Don't you tell me to sleep!

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:13.830
What the heck, Chihaya?
The teacher's gonna come back!

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:14.710
Taichi!

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:16.380
Tai... Ea...

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:21.340
Ea... Ea... Ea... Ea... Ea...

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:22.860
It's Dr. Harada.

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:31.090
He's representing East Japan.

00:19:34.710 --> 00:19:35.820
And for West Japan—

00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:39.430
Michiru-chan! I need my battery back!
Where's my phone?!

00:19:39.430 --> 00:19:40.440
What?!

00:19:41.870 --> 00:19:42.940
R-Really?

00:19:44.240 --> 00:19:45.610
Really?

00:19:47.950 --> 00:19:51.060
D-Did Dr. Harada really...

00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:57.540
Which one are you going to
root for in the play-off?

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:02.230
Which one? Dr. Harada, obvio—

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:06.460
He's amazing, isn't he?

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:10.770
<i>The West Japan representative is... Arata?!</i>

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:16.300
<i>Dr. Harada and Arata are gonna 
compete to be the challenger?!</i>

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:29.070
Yo, Mashima! What just 
happened with Ayase-san?

00:20:29.070 --> 00:20:32.320
You just had to draw attention to 
yourself, coming here late...

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:34.570
Huh?!

00:20:34.570 --> 00:20:36.020
M-Mashima?!

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:36.940
Hey!

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:38.960
Uh, guys, he's all right.

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:41.660
He's just sleeping.

00:20:42.030 --> 00:20:46.340
He's a hundred times more tired 
than any of us after today.

00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:49.360
There we go.

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:52.190
Desktomu's such a manly man.

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:53.110
We'll help.

00:20:53.110 --> 00:20:54.540
Lay out a futon.

00:20:56.880 --> 00:21:00.640
<i>Mashima... It would've been great
if you'd come here victorious.</i>

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:03.800
<i>I know karuta isn't that simple.</i>

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:04.980
<i>But...</i>

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:11.210
<i>It would've been great if you'd won.</i>

00:21:17.250 --> 00:21:20.420
<b>Mailbox 
